{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790983791,"nonce":"PDhypwXHyG6hpwO/TzPYL9dadOY=","title":"caribou_abi has no Param for an optional enum argument","message":"x-idl now accepts a method argument declared `Option\u003cEnum\u003cT\u003e\u003e` (x-idl git-bug 358ed3a0ef18fa10e786b5bfd61bf8fafc6672c77e98a7c1e03d93171ae9a4ec). For HashLink and Rayzor it lowers to the enum's native value, with i32::MIN for none. For Caribou, the generated plugin method keeps the declared type, as `fn setTheme(\u0026Window, Option\u003cEnum\u003cTheme\u003e\u003e)` in `caribou_abi::plugin!`. caribou_abi implements `Param` for `Enum\u003cT\u003e` but not for `Option\u003cEnum\u003cT\u003e\u003e`, so a Caribou build of such a declaration fails to compile at the plugin table's `const _: extern \"C\" fn(...)` check.\n\nThe first user is xwindow's `Window.setTheme(theme: Option\u003cEnum\u003cTheme\u003e\u003e)` (winit's set_theme; none means follow the system), which cb_window will need once it moves onto xwindow.\n\nNeeded: `impl\u003cT: PluginEnum\u003e Param for Option\u003cEnum\u003cT\u003e\u003e` with a representation that crosses `extern \"C\"` (Enum\u003cT\u003e as an FFI-safe pointer, or a tag the frontends read as a nullable enum), and the frontends' (Wren, Zyntax) handling of a null argument for it.","files":null}]}